    "text": "Middleware & Pipeline System Subatom's middleware and pipeline system provides multiple points for intercepting and modifying requests and responses. Understand the differences between middleware, transformers, interceptors, and serializers. Middleware Basics Middleware are functions that have access to request and response objects and can modify them or respond early. Middleware Signature Global Middleware Global middleware runs on every request: Path-Scoped Middleware Middleware attached to a path prefix: Route-Scoped Middleware Middleware attached to specific routes: Common Middleware Patterns Logging Middleware Authentication Middleware CORS Middleware Rate Limiting Middleware Body Parser Middleware Error Middleware Error middleware has 4 parameters for handling errors: Basic Error Handler Multi-Level Error Handling Pipeline Modifiers Beyond middleware, Subatom provides transformers, interceptors, and serializers for lifecycle hooks. Transformers Transformers hook into request/response lifecycle with priority-based ordering: beforeRequest Runs after middleware, before route handler: afterRequest Runs after route handler completes: beforeResponse Runs after serialization, before sending to client: afterResponse Runs after response sent for logging, cleanup : Interceptors Interceptors run before route handler with middleware-style next pattern: Intercept Pattern Serializers Serializers handle final response formatting: Multiple Format Serializers Pipeline Execution Order Best Practices 1. Order Matters 2. Use Priority for Transformers 3. Error Handling in Middleware 4. Short-Circuit on Error 5. Middleware Composition Common Pitfalls ❌ Not Calling next ❌ Calling next Multiple Times ❌ Mixing Middleware and Transformers Next Steps - Learn about Error Handling ./error-handling.md in middleware - Explore Context ./context.md in route handlers - Implement Validation ./validation.md middleware - Set up Production Best Practices ./best-practices.md"
