    "text": "Request Validation Subatom validates request body, query, params, headers, and files through its route schema system. Subatom Infer is the native ecosystem validator, and the validation layer can consume schemas that expose the supported Standard Schema protocol. Overview Validation in Subatom: - Supports schemas implementing the supported Standard Schema protocol - Validates body, query, params, headers, and files - Performs type coercion and transformation - Returns detailed validation errors - Provides full TypeScript type inference Supported Schema Protocol subatom-infer is the native validation package in the Subatom ecosystem. For other validators, verify that the version you use exposes the Standard Schema interface expected by the installed Subatom version. Basic Validation Body Validation Query Validation Parameter Validation Headers Validation Type Inference Subatom infers request types from your validation schemas: Advanced Validation Conditional Validation Cross-Field Validation Coercion and Transformation File Validation Single File Upload Multiple Files Upload File with Body Validation Validation Error Handling When validation fails, a UnprocessableEntityError is thrown: Schema Organization Reusable Schemas Schema Composition Production Best Practices 1. Validate Everything 2. Type-Safe Query Params 3. Detailed Error Messages 4. Optional vs Required Fields Common Pitfalls ❌ Not Validating Query Params ❌ Not Cleaning Up Uploaded Files ❌ Overly Broad Error Catching Next Steps - Learn about Error Handling ./error-handling.md for validation errors - Explore File Upload ./file-upload.md for advanced file handling - Set up Middleware ./middleware.md for request preprocessing - Read Production Best Practices ./best-practices.md for scaling"
